  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-tenacity-and-ravage-state",
      "title": {
        "en": "What is Tenacity and Ravage State"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_30075_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30075_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30075_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Sereniel's Afterglow, Tenacity Damage and Homing Lazers"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Afterglow is Serenial's Unique Buff\nNext Attack Card: +1 Tenacity Damage and +50% Dmg on Ravaged Enemies\nAfterglow is consumed on every attack card that uses it, no limit of stacks\nTenacity Damage is another way of Damaging Tenacity\n1 Tenacity Damage is equal to 1 Bar of Tenacity\nWeakness does not change the ammount of Tenacity Damage\nHoming Lazers are Serenial's main pay off for Ravage\nThey Move themself into hand on Ravage to be used again"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_30075_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_30075_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Tenacity is the Bar Underneath some enemies\nTenacity is broken up into Segments, different on each enemy\nNot all Enemies have Tenacity Bars to be Ravage\nTenacity is decreased by Attack cards in different ammounts\nExamples:\n2 Cost Attack against Weakness = 2 Full Bars of Tenacity\n1 Cost Attack against Weakness = 1 Full Bar of Tenacity\n0 Cost Attack against Weakness = 1/2 Bar of Tenacity\nIf the enemy is not weak, characters do 1/3rd of the usual damage to Tenacity\nNon Targeted Attacks deal 1/2 of the usual damage to Tenacity\nRavage is the state an enemy enters if their Tenacity is Broken\nRavaging an enemy grants the team +1 AP and delays enemy action count +1\nCharacters unless they specifically have an Anti Ravage effects\nDo not deal extra damage to enemies that are Ravaged"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
